&lt;p&gt;It started with a photo I saw: the sun rising right out of Guishan Island.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My first thought was, where do you have to stand to get that shot? Guishan Island sits off the Yilan coast, so from any point on the shoreline it takes up a certain slice of sky, and the direction the sun rises changes every day. Getting those two to line up should be something you can calculate.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>